# PROVENANCE: measured from a factory-fresh genuine DESFire EV3 2K with Proxmark3 on 2026-11-01
# (random UID; PICC master key at its all-zero default). Same card and batch as
# hardware_physical_ev3_2k_value_rights.vec.
# PROVISIONAL BATCH "value-rights-2026-11-01": carries `capture-batch: value-rights-2026-11-01` and
# `capture-status: provisional`, so it can be thrown away with the rest of the batch if the card
# proves faulty (see docs/capture-batches.md).
#
# What this measures: how ISO UPDATE BINARY and ISO READ BINARY interact with an open native
# transaction (a staged WriteData on a backup file, or a staged Debit on a value file). The
# application has a value file 4, a backup data file 5 and a standard data file 6, all free
# access, the last two with ISO ids 1005 and 1006. Each section's pattern differs so a leftover
# from an earlier section cannot be mistaken for its own result.
# Observed:
#   * A successful ISO UPDATE BINARY publishes the open transaction: the staged write and a staged
#     Debit are committed along with it (a later CommitTransaction or AbortTransaction answers 0C,
#     "nothing to do", and the balance already shows the Debit).
#   * An ISO UPDATE BINARY aimed at a backup file is written at once; the native read shows it
#     before any commit and CommitTransaction has nothing to commit.
#   * A FAILING ISO UPDATE BINARY (offset past the end, 6985) discards the open transaction.
#   * A successful ISO READ BINARY leaves the staged write alone; CommitTransaction publishes it.
name: genuine EV3 2K ISO UPDATE BINARY and READ BINARY against an open native transaction (provisional batch)
case-id: hardware-physical-ev3-2k-iso-update-binary-transaction
origin: physical-card
capture-batch: value-rights-2026-11-01
capture-status: provisional
feature-version: 6
source: physical-card-proxmark3
requires: backup-files
uid: 04112233445566
picc-generation: EV3
picc-storage: 2048
picc-key-settings-1: 0F
picc-key-settings-2: 01
picc-key-len: 16
picc-auth-mode: D40
picc-hardware-version: 04010133001605
picc-software-version: 04010103001605

# fixture: application 123456 with value file 4, backup data file 5 (ISO id 1005) and standard data file 6 (ISO id 1006), all free access
field-off
scan
exchange native CA1234560F2200E1 => 00
exchange native 5A123456 => 00
exchange native CC0400EEEE00000000E80300006400000001 => 00
exchange native CB05051000EEEE100000 => 00
exchange native CD06061000EEEE100000 => 00

# staged native WriteData on backup file 5, then ISO UPDATE BINARY on standard file 6, then CommitTransaction
field-off
scan
exchange native 5A123456 => 00
exchange iso-apdu 00A4000C021006 => 9000
exchange native 3D05000000040000A1A1A1A1 => 00
exchange iso-apdu 00D600000411111111 => 9000
exchange native C7 => 0C
exchange native BD05000000000000 => 00A1A1A1A1000000000000000000000000
exchange native BD06000000000000 => 0011111111000000000000000000000000
exchange native 6C04 => 0064000000

# staged native WriteData on backup file 5, then ISO UPDATE BINARY on standard file 6, then AbortTransaction
field-off
scan
exchange native 5A123456 => 00
exchange iso-apdu 00A4000C021006 => 9000
exchange native 3D05000000040000A2A2A2A2 => 00
exchange iso-apdu 00D600000422222222 => 9000
exchange native A7 => 0C
exchange native BD05000000000000 => 00A2A2A2A2000000000000000000000000
exchange native BD06000000000000 => 0022222222000000000000000000000000
exchange native 6C04 => 0064000000

# staged native Debit of 5, then ISO UPDATE BINARY on standard file 6, then GetValue, AbortTransaction, GetValue
field-off
scan
exchange native 5A123456 => 00
exchange iso-apdu 00A4000C021006 => 9000
exchange native DC0405000000 => 00
exchange iso-apdu 00D600000433333333 => 9000
exchange native 6C04 => 005F000000
exchange native A7 => 0C
exchange native 6C04 => 005F000000

# ISO UPDATE BINARY directly on backup file 5: native read before commit, CommitTransaction, native read
field-off
scan
exchange native 5A123456 => 00
exchange iso-apdu 00A4000C021005 => 9000
exchange iso-apdu 00D600000444444444 => 9000
exchange native BD05000000000000 => 0044444444000000000000000000000000
exchange native C7 => 0C
exchange native BD05000000000000 => 0044444444000000000000000000000000

# ISO UPDATE BINARY directly on backup file 5: native read before abort, AbortTransaction, native read
field-off
scan
exchange native 5A123456 => 00
exchange iso-apdu 00A4000C021005 => 9000
exchange iso-apdu 00D600000455555555 => 9000
exchange native BD05000000000000 => 0055555555000000000000000000000000
exchange native A7 => 0C
exchange native BD05000000000000 => 0055555555000000000000000000000000

# staged native WriteData on backup file 5, then a failing ISO UPDATE BINARY (offset past the end), then CommitTransaction
field-off
scan
exchange native 5A123456 => 00
exchange iso-apdu 00A4000C021006 => 9000
exchange native 3D05000000040000A6A6A6A6 => 00
exchange iso-apdu 00D600200466666666 => 6985
exchange native C7 => 0C
exchange native BD05000000000000 => 0055555555000000000000000000000000
exchange native BD06000000000000 => 0033333333000000000000000000000000
exchange native 6C04 => 005F000000

# staged native WriteData on backup file 5, then a successful ISO READ BINARY, then CommitTransaction
field-off
scan
exchange native 5A123456 => 00
exchange iso-apdu 00A4000C021006 => 9000
exchange native 3D05000000040000A7A7A7A7 => 00
exchange iso-apdu 00B0000004 => 333333339000
exchange native C7 => 00
exchange native BD05000000000000 => 00A7A7A7A7000000000000000000000000
exchange native BD06000000000000 => 0033333333000000000000000000000000
exchange native 6C04 => 005F000000
